<report>
<title>Bonferroni comparison</title>

<p>Variable A: @var_a<br />
Variable B: @var_b<br />
Mean A - Mean B = @{a-b:roundu}<br />
Estimated std. error = @{std_err:roundu}<br />
Number of groups = @groups<br />
@{pc:round2}% confidence interval = @{from:roundu} to @{to:roundu}<br />
Bonferroni-adjusted (simultaneous) @{pc:round2}% confidence interval for @comp = @{adj_from:roundu} to @{adj_to:roundu} (each comparison at @{adj_pc:round2}%)</p>

<p>t = @{t:roundu}<br />
df = @df<br />
<pval>@{p:pval}</pval></p>

<p>Bonferroni critical P for @comp = @{bonf:roundu}</p>
</report>
